      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are two short monologue options for your screenplay.\n\n**For the \"Reasonable Traditionalist\" (wise, calm mentor):**\n\"Now, I see the strong opinions here, and I understand the passion for the town we love. But a strong foundation, like a good well, requires a steady, predictable source, not a sudden, forceful surge of change. We must honor the way things have always been, because that is the strength that truly grounds us in this place.\"\n\n**For the \"Radical Progressive\" (intense, passionate):**\n\"'Strong foundation' is a polite way of saying you prefer the status *quo* because it benefits *your* side of the world. This town is built on an inequality that we can no longer pretend to ignore, and ' steady' is just the language of the powerful to keep the progress of the many in the can. We have to tear down the old framework to build one that actually *breathes* for everyone here, now and in the future.\"",
